{"uid":"1b1e6cc57edef96d","name":"test_normalize_tool_and_call_result_against_real_mcp_types","fullName":"tests.test_mcp_gateway_units#test_normalize_tool_and_call_result_against_real_mcp_types","historyId":"59939f3a4c91959eb2cbab412339793c","time":{"start":1789882106851,"stop":1789882106852,"duration":1},"description":"The two tests above use ``SimpleNamespace`` fixtures the test author\n    names to match whatever the source reads -- so a future rename of the\n    *real* SDK field can't fail here even if source and fixture drift apart,\n    which is exactly how ``inputSchema``/``outputSchema``/``structuredContent``\n    silently became dead reads under mcp 2.x (``getattr`` with a default never\n    raises; every discovered tool's real schema and every structured tool\n    result quietly dropped to ``{}``/``None``/``[]`` instead). This constructs\n    the genuine ``mcp.types`` objects instead, so a future SDK rename fails\n    this test rather than passing it by construction.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>The two tests above use <code>SimpleNamespace</code> fixtures the test author<br />\nnames to match whatever the source reads -- so a future rename of the<br />\n<em>real</em> SDK field can't fail here even if source and fixture drift apart,<br />\nwhich is exactly how <code>inputSchema</code>/<code>outputSchema</code>/<code>structuredContent</code><br />\nsilently became dead reads under mcp 2.x (<code>getattr</code> with a default never<br />\nraises; every discovered tool's real schema and every structured tool<br />\nresult quietly dropped to <code>{}</code>/<code>None</code>/<code>[]</code> instead). This constructs<br />\nthe genuine <code>mcp.types</code> objects instead, so a future SDK rename fails<br />\nthis test rather than passing it by construction.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1789881